WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.920
Some of the most common
questions I get

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:05.320
are about the dosage
and type of vitamin B12.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.334
Check out the video
for some answers.

00:00:07.441 --> 00:00:14.226
"The Optimal Vitamin B12 Dosage and Type"

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.120
Universal improvement of B12 status
appears “to be a nutritional

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.960
imperative with possibly
profound beneficial effects,”

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.720
particularly at the bookends
of life—at old age and infancy.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.520
I’ve explained the rationale
for my recommendations

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.360
to take vitamin B12 supplements
once a week or once a day,

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.520
or alternately eat sufficient
daily B12-fortified foods.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.560
But for those over age 65 those
guidelines go out the window.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.000
The recommendations change
to everyone taking

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.280
a high daily dose of
1,000 mcg every day.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.760
Starting at age 50 everyone,
meat-eaters and vegans alike,

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.520
should be taking B12 supplements
or eating B12-fortified foods.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:05.200
But over age 65, 50 a day may not do it.
Even 100 a day doesn’t seem sufficient.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.160
Researchers investigated three
doses and found that most

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.640
didn’t normalize their MMA until
after the 1,000 microgram dose.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.320
(MMA suppression is a
measure of B12 sufficiency.)

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:22.000
But they just tested 25, 100, and 1,000.
Maybe 250 or 500 would do it?

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.880
Researchers set out to find an
adequate dose at that age,

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:29.840
and it seems we need at least about
650 to 1,000 a day in most people,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.680
hence my 1,000 a day
recommendation after age 65.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.240
OK, what about the other
end of the life cycle?

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:41.120
The consequences of B12 deficiency
and insufficiency can be

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.120
devastating in
infancy and childhood,

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:46.360
and this is not just a problem
for plant-based pregnancies.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:49.560
“Vitamin B-12 insufﬁciency during
pregnancy is common

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.600
even in nonvegetarian populations.”

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:55.920
About a quarter of all pregnant
women aren’t getting enough B12,

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.200
and that number rises to nearly
one in three by the third trimester.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.600
But, insufficiency isn’t as
bad as frank deficiency,

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.080
which can manifest in
cases like cerebral atrophy,

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.960
meaning brain shrinkage,

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:14.520
in a “Vitamin B12-deficient
Infant of a Vegetarian Mother.”

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.440
Thankfully, even severe
brain atrophy can be

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.360
substantially reversed with
B12 supplementation,

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:25.240
but better not to become
deficient in the first place.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:28.360
The solution proposed by a group
of French pediatricians

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:31.840
is to recommend against
raising vegan kids at all,

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.480
since B12 supplementation is
necessary. And they’re not alone.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.840
To vegan or not to vegan.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:42.400
In 2016, two professional
organizations, the U.S. Academy

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.080
of Nutrition and Dietetics and
the German Nutrition Society,

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.800
issued conﬂicting statements.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.120
The U.S. Academy said that
even strictly plant-based diets

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.200
are appropriate for all
stages of the life cycle,

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.360
whereas the German group
echoed the French group,

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.680
saying since you have to take B12
we can’t recommend a vegan diet

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:05.640
for pregnant women, lactating women,
infants, children, or adolescents.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:09.440
To confuse the matter further,
the American Academy of Pediatrics

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:12.680
appeared to have it both ways;
in one place repeating

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:15.880
the U.S. Academy’s position, while
in another place it stated that

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.920
vegan diets should not
be recommended for children.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.960
But I think they’re just
saying the same thing.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:25.600
Everyone agrees that a non-B12
supplemented plant-based diet

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:30.320
is a bad idea—that’s part of what
the U.S. Academy means

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:32.040
by “well-planned.”

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:36.040
Everyone eating plant-based,
but especially pregnant

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:41.080
and breastfeeding women, must
ensure a regular, reliable source

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:46.080
of vitamin B12, meaning B12
supplements or B12-fortified foods.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:50.840
But then you may be able to
get the best of both worlds.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:53.200
That’s why there are
reviews with titles like this:

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.520
plant-based pregnancies:
danger or panacea?

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.960
Danger if you don’t take your B12,
but “following a plant-[based] diet

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:04.000
during pregnancy may be protective
against the development of preeclampsia,

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.320
pre-gravid obesity, and minimize the
exposure to [DNA-damaging] agents.”

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.440
It may also protect our newborns
“from the onset of pediatric diseases,

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.720
such as pediatric wheezing,
diabetes, neural tube defects,

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:20.480
orofacial clefts, and some
pediatric tumors.”

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.720
“Vegan pregnant women
have a lower-than-average

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:26.200
rate of cesarean section,
less postpartum depression,

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:29.840
and lower neonatal and
maternal mortality,

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.080
with no complications or negative
outcomes that are higher than average.”

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.160
In addition, a lower incidence
of what used to be called toxemia,

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.400
a potentially dangerous pregnancy
complication known as preeclampsia.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:46.440
“Overall, plant-based diets
seem to confer protection to both

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:50.400
mothers and newborns” by not
only “reducing the risk of several

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:55.960
pregnancy-related issues”, but
decreasing the risk of childhood disease.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.560
“Children following plant-based
diets might have a lower risk

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.760
of developing obesity,” obviously
are less exposed to drugs

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.360
used in animal production,
and a favorable

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:08.200
anti-inﬂammatory proﬁle
of cell-signaling factors.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:13.240
But again, everyone on a plant-based
diet has to get enough B12.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:15.000
Pregnant and breastfeeding
women can just follow

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.600
my 50 micrograms a day
recommendation for nonpregnant adults,

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:21.960
or 2,000 a week, though they
suggest breaking up those doses

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.680
into two halves to boost absorption.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:30.160
After infants are weaned, they
can start on 5 micrograms a day;

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:34.520
from ages 4 through 10 they can
take half the adult dose of 25 a day;

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.520
and then at age 11 they can
take 50 a day or 2,000 a week.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.480
You don’t have to worry
about taking too much.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:45.280
It’s water-soluble and you’ll
just end up with expensive pee.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.760
I've talked about the optimal dose of
vitamin B12 supplements for adults,

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.480
as well as in childhood, pregnancy,
and old age to prevent

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:55.760
vitamin B12 deficiency. But
what if you already have it?

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:59.200
How much do you
have to take to treat it?

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:02.880
Your doctor might want you
to get vitamin B12 injections,

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:07.160
but oral B12, even for those
who can't absorb it well,

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:11.320
has long been considered one
of medicine's best kept secrets.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:15.160
It's now considered well-known that
orally administered B12 supplements

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:21.520
are as effective in overcoming deficiency
states as intramuscular injections

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:25.480
when you get up to taking
1,000 micrograms a day.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.920
How long do you have
to take 1,000 a day for?

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:32.080
It depends on how low
your levels start out.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:35.360
Because B12 status in
pregnancy is so critical,

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.800
there is a suggestion that plant-based
women get it checked

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:41.880
throughout pregnancy and to adjust
supplementation as necessary.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.760
This is how much you
should take if you're low.

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:47.560
Note the recommendations for
pregnant and breast-feeding women

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:51.080
are the same as everyone
else over the age of 10.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:55.520
So if you're a teen or adult diagnosed
with vitamin B12 deficiency,

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:59.400
you'd take 1,000 micrograms
a day for one to four months,

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:03.320
depending on how low you
start out, before going back

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:07.440
to a regular maintenance dose
of 50 a day or 2,000 a week,

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:11.560
with toddlers and small
children taking smaller doses.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:16.000
There are two main types on the
market though: methylcobalamin,

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.080
marketed as methyl B12,
and cyanocobalamin,

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.840
typically marketed as
just vitamin B12.

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:25.560
Methyl is more expensive so
it must be better, right?

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:32.080
Wrong. Cyanocobalamin is the most
used form due to its high stability.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:35.680
See, methylcobalamin is less
stable than cyanocobalamin,

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:39.400
and it is particularly susceptible
to photodecomposition,

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:43.080
meaning destruction from
being exposed to light.

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:46.920
There's no advantage to using the
light-sensitive forms of cobalamin,

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:51.720
such as methyl B12, instead of the
stable cyano forms, which are readily

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:56.000
converted in the body into the type
you need, where you need it.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.640
The one major exception
may be kidney failure though.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:04.080
Methylcobalamin may be better for
those with impaired kidney function.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:07.120
It's been speculated that oral
methylcobalamin or injected

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:10.440
hydroxycobalamin may also
be preferable in smokers,

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.760
though it has yet to be confirmed.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:16.280
Because methylcobalamin is less
stable, you'd probably want to take

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:20.080
much higher doses. So for example,
in those with kidney failure, you'd be

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:24.200
taking one to two thousand micrograms
a day, compared to just 50 micrograms

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:27.840
of cyanocobalamin in someone
with normal kidney function.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.600
Another reason to use the
cyanocobalamin, as opposed to

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:37.360
the more expensive kinds, is that it has
a track record of safety and efficacy,

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:40.640
whereas, for example, in one study
even up to 2,000 micrograms a day

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:45.040
of methylcobalamin wasn't enough
to correct vitamin B12 deficiency

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.320
in one of three vegans
they tested it on.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.600
The bottom line is that so-called
coenzyme forms of B12,

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:56.320
like methyl B12 and adenyl B12,
also known as adenosyl B12,

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:01.040
are not likely to be superior to
cyanocobalamin, which is more stable.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:05.800
Cyanocobalamin appears to be best
suited for oral supplementation,

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:10.120
which is why I specify its
use in my recommendations.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:13.080
Note I also recommend ideally
taking it separately

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:16.680
as a chewable, sublingual,
or liquid supplement.

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:19.560
Why can't you just get it as part
of a multivitamin or something?

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:23.160
Because various vitamins and
minerals mixed into the same pill

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:28.720
can destroy active B12, forming B12
analogues—B12-look-alikes that (not)

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:34.480
only can our body not use, the
analogues can be potentially harmful

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:38.280
because they can inhibit the
transport of what little B12 is left.

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:41.720
That's why using multivitamins
can even be counterproductive

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:45.880
for the supplementation of vitamin
B12. And this isn't just in theory.

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:49.800
There was a tragic case of severe
vitamin B12 deficiency in an infant

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:52.880
born to a vegan mother who thought
she was doing everything right

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:55.680
taking a multivitamin
that contained B12,

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:59.120
though it may have also just
been inadequate dose.

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:02.720
Why chewable or sublingual?

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:06.240
Absorption is boosted when
the B12 mixes with saliva,

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:09.640
since you secrete a B12 binding
protein from your salivary glands

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:13.760
that helps transport B12 safely
through the digestive tract.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:19.160
Having people chew a tablet of B12 and
their B12 levels go up 10 times more

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:23.440
than just simply swallowing the
exact same pill. Check it out.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:27.800
Vegans boosted out of deficiency
chewing a B12 supplement,

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:31.160
but nothing in those who
just swallowed it whole.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:33.680
Maybe they had some sort of
absorption problem or something?

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:36.600
No, because then if you tell them
to start chewing it instead

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:40.840
of swallowing it whole, their
levels shoot right up as well.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:45.760
In my latest book How Not to Diet,
I suggest a third option to B12-

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:49.160
fortified foods and supplements:
brushing twice daily with

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:53.800
a B12-fortified toothpaste,
specifically this brand,

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:56.640
which was put to the test
in two double-blind,

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:58.640
randomized, placebo-controlled studies.

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:01.800
Participants were instructed to use
the toothpaste two times a day

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:05.240
for two minutes at a time, and indeed,
were able to correct the markers

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:10.200
of B12 insufficiency in the blood
of vegans and among the elderly,

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:16.120
but that was on average. Unfortunately,
it didn't work in every last person,

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:19.240
which is why it's not included
in my recommendations.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:22.120
Though, look, if you get your levels
tested before and after brushing

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:26.880
for a few months and they go up, then
you could presumably stick with it.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:31.840
In summary, vitamin B12 deficiency
is not to be messed around with,

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:36.000
with the potential to cause a wide
range of disorders of the gut,

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.120
blood, brain, and
nervous system.

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:42.200
With the ever-increasing demand
for cleanliness in our food chain—

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.160
which is a very good thing—

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:48.680
it is of special importance that we
secure a regular reliable source,

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:52.520
and the safest, cheapest, healthiest
source is B12 supplements

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:56.247
or green-light B12-fortified foods.

